Subject: Tools: drawbench and the golden streams (tools/dev.mk check)

What the work on a draw's CPU cost is measured and held with:

- tools/drawbench.cpp: frames a window server draws at the phone's size, recorded on the fake GPU, the time inside the
  draw calls alone taken a draw, the heap allocations in them counted. Scenes A-H, P, Q, R are the performance
  audit's (the core's interface, hand-made programs); J, K, L drive the C interface the plug-in drives, with linked
  programs, vertex and index buffers, uniforms bound at multiples of 8, a stage of ten texture slots with one bound,
  fetches, two colour outputs, programs changing from draw to draw; S, T (--stages DIR) do the same with the stages of
  a phone's own cache. --cold KB empties the processor's caches of the driver before each draw.
- the golden streams: FakeGpu::submitHook hands every submission over as it arrives, tests/golden.hpp sums the words
  the command processor reads (bodies each time they are called) and, apart, the bytes every indirect load names (a
  draw's tables, the programs). `drawbench --golden` prints a line a scene, `tests --golden` a line a test;
  tests/golden/ holds them for both chips and `make -f tools/dev.mk check` compares. A change that is meant to leave
  the stream as it was is held to that word for word. (One test and one scene whose addresses the threads decide
  are counted, not summed.)
- include/hakios-metal/testing.hpp: hakios_metal_program_from_stages, a program as the C interface holds one made
  from two Stages without the compiler, so that a build without Mesa drives the plug-in's own entry points.
- tools/dev.mk: the tests and drawbench built object by object, for either chip's constants (CHIP=a610).


